1. Overview
DonateHub is a lightweight donation marketplace web application.
Core features

User registration + login
Create donation listings (title, description, category, condition, image)
Browse and search available donation items
Message donors about items (implemented using Server‑Sent Events)

2. Business problem
Many households have usable items they no longer need, while others cannot easily afford replacements. A simple platform for local donation reduces waste and helps communities.
3. Stakeholders

Donors: post items and coordinate handover
Recipients: browse items and request via message
Community groups/charities: source items
Admins (future): moderation and reporting

4. Value

Lower landfill waste and carbon impact
Improves access to essential household goods
Strengthens community support networks

5. Non-functional requirements

Simple, lo-fi UI (fast to learn)
Runs locally in development
No extra backend npm dependencies beyond: express, dotenv, sequelize, mysql2

6. Architecture
6.1 High-level

Frontend: minimal React (via CDN) + Context for global state
Backend: Express MVC + Sequelize ORM
Database: MySQL (Workbench) at localhost:3306
